  "hints": [
    "A literal is already a &str.",
    "Watch the trailing semicolon in the body."
  ],
  "explanation": "A `String` does not pass where `&str` is expected (E0308) - but two fixes work: the literal `\"ferris\"` is already a `&str`, and `&String::from(\"ferris\")` converts through deref coercion. Both earn the star; the literal is simply shorter. In the body, `to_uppercase()` returns the owned String the signature promises - with a semicolon the body returns `()`, and returning `name` alone is a `&str` where a `String` is due.",
